Pages = {573-583},
Month = {OCT},
Abstract = {This article aims to understand the process of socio reinterpretation of
   the bay - Bahia - Brazil, through the inclusion of tourism in order to
   propose strategies for sustainable tourism planning. It is understood
   that tourism, as economic activity and as a social phenomenon, brings
   the social, cultural and environmental consequences and / or positive
   (Bomfim, 2006; Dias; 2003; Yazigi, 2008). From this perspective,
   understanding the perception of the main actors on the production of
   tourist place, the bay is to seek clues that might enable the planning
   of sustainable tourism. It draws on this study a qualitative approach /
   interpretation. The results indicate that the redefinition of the area
   of the bay, the fishermen, and merchants cabaneiros, affective is the
   perception of them, to the extent that changes in the dimensions of
   environmental, social and cultural otherness involves a relationship
   between these subjects and visitors. Accordingly, a participatory
   planning can guide actions for sustainability of tourism.},
