   Nature and Parks Authority, Society for Protection of Nature in Israel,
   ``Yarok Ba'Lev{''} NGO, the Haifa Educational Zoo, the Municipality of
   Haifa, and Gazelle Valley urban Nature Park for their essential
   cooperation and assistance in carrying out the surveys and the
   management of the data from the Haifa Salamander survey, and to the
   Haifa community of the SPNI in particular for their help and support of
   the Haifa Salamander project over the years. We thank Yael Hammerman,
   Avishai Shoresh, Noemi Cohen Kappach, and Chen Chaim for their help and
   support in carrying out the toad surveys, analyzing preliminary
   datasets, and involvement in various phases of the citizen science
   project. The study was inspired by the life's work of the late Prof.
   Leon Blaustein, and was initiated by O.R. while working in his lab. We
   dedicate this study to Leon's memory, in recognition of his lifelong
   contributions to ecology, evolution, and the conservation of salamanders
   and wildlife more broadly, and the spirit of curiosity and enthusiasm
   that guided his work.},
